of the Anopheles gambiae complex</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><year>1987</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>37</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2886070</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fischer</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Erickson</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Fischer</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Fuchs</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Rao</surname><given-names>RU</given-names></name><name><surname>Christensen</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Weil</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Persistence of Brugia malayi DNA in vector and non-vector mosquitoes: implications for xenomonitoring and transmission monitoring of lymphatic filariasis</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><year>2007</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>502</fpage><lpage>507</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17360875</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>